1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
One tap. Watch where her password actually goes.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,000
It does not take her password. It opens Microsoft’s page instead.

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,800
It goes to Microsoft Entra ID. Your servers are not in this step.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,600
Multi-factor. A stolen password on its own is now worth nothing.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,400
Not her password. A pass, signed by Microsoft, good for 60 minutes.

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,200
On its own. It does not call anyone, so it costs microseconds.

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,000
Your API reaches the database with a managed identity.

8
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,800
To Microsoft. Everything after that was a signed token.
